{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795452825,"nonce":"Yvs46xQP8Yu+nvNuIyiq+eAHj6Y=","title":"A parametric initial state on a periodic transient is not reduced with the march","message":"A nodal jno.np.parameter (or any trainable) in the initial condition of a transient with periodic ties: fem.solve(values=...) fails on the first step with a shape mismatch between the full nodal state and the reduced main-DOF state, linear and nonlinear alike. _reduce_transient_block_periodic restricts the static state0 but hands the block's state0_fn through unchanged, so the state re-formed from the runtime args stays on the full layout. Repro: tests/test_fem_periodic_transient.py::test_periodic_transient_marches_from_an_initial_state_given_at_solve_time.","files":null}]}